 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_nMB9FhY9dsj2cpQy",
   "name": "Increasing the Carbon Chain Length",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Increasing the Carbon Chain Length"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- If we need to increase the chain length we can use **Grignard reagents**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Preparing Grignard reagents"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- A halogenoalkane is dissolved in dry ether and reacted with magnesium to produce the reactive Grignard reagent\n- If 1-iodoethane is reacted with magnesium, **ethyl magnesium iodide** is produced\n- This is an example of a Grignard reagent"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**I + Mg → CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**MgI  **"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- These compounds are highly reactive and the alkyl group (R group) can be considered to have a negative charge, therefore it can behave as a nucleophile\n\n  - **R**<sup>**-**</sup>**[**<sup>**+**</sup>**MgI]**\n- Carbonyl compounds and carbon dioxide will react with Grignard reagents to give different products as part of a two-step reaction (specific reaction details and mechanisms are not required at this level)\n\n  - An initial product is formed during an addition reaction\n  - Dilute acid is then added to hydrolyse this initial product"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Reactions of Grignard with carbonyl compounds"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Grignard reagents react with **methanal** to produce a **primary alcohol **"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**RMgI + HCHO **$\\overset{H_{2}O}{\\rightarrow}$** RCH**<sub>**2**</sub>**OH + Mg(OH)I**"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- For example, methanal can react with ethyl magnesium iodide to produce **propanol**"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**MgI  + HCHO **$\\overset{H_{2}O}{\\rightarrow}$** CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**OH + Mg(OH)I**"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- They also can react with **longer chain aldehydes** to produce **secondary alcohols**\n- For example, ethanal can react with ethyl magnesium iodide to produce butan-2-ol"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**MgI  + CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CHO  **$\\overset{H_{2}O}{\\rightarrow}$** CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**CH(OH)CH**<sub>**3 **</sub>**+ Mg(OH)I**"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Ketones** are also able to react with Grignard reagents producing a tertiary alcohol\n- For example, propanone can react with ethyl magnesium iodide to produce **2-methylbutan-2-ol **"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**MgI  + CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**COCH**<sub>**3**</sub>** **$\\overset{H_{2}O}{\\rightarrow}$** CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**C(CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**)(OH)CH**<sub>**3 **</sub>**+ Mg(OH)I**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Reactions of Grignard reagents with carbon dioxide"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- This reaction will produce a carboxylic acid"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**MgI  + CO**<sub>**2**</sub>** **$\\overset{H_{2}O}{\\rightarrow}$** CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**CH**<sub>**2**</sub>**COOH + Mg(OH)I**"
  }
 ]
}